/T (\(a\) The use of oil, grease or other lubricants on the body, or personal equipment is strictly forbidden.  \(b\) Baby powder, resin, talc or magnesium carbonates are the only substances that may be added to the body and attire, but not to the wraps.  \(c\) The use of any form of adhesive on the underside of footwear is strictly forbidden. This applies to any built-in adhesive, e.g. glass paper, emery cloth, etc. and to include resin and magnesium carbonate. A spray of water is acceptable.  \(d\) No foreign substances may be applied to the powerlifting equipment. This takes into account all substances other than that which may be used periodically as a sterile agent in the cleaning of the bar, bench, or platform.  \(e\) Light protective guards between sock and shin may be worn.  \(f\) Athletes are allowed to wear necklaces and similar accessories. No part of the necklace or accessory shall be placed In the mouth while on the platform. A pendant or charm may be worn either over or under the T-shrt; however, If deemed to create a safety concern or Interfere with the lift, the Referee may require It to be secured under the T-shirt or removed.)
/E (\(a\) The use of oil, grease or other lubricants on the body, or personal equipment is strictly forbidden.  \(b\) Baby powder, resin, talc or magnesium carbonates are the only substances that may be added to the body and attire, but not to the wraps.  \(c\) The use of any form of adhesive on the underside of footwear is strictly forbidden. This applies to any built-in adhesive, e.g. glass paper, emery cloth, etc. and to include resin and magnesium carbonate. A spray of water is acceptable.  \(d\) No foreign substances may be applied to the powerlifting equipment. This takes into account all substances other than that which may be used periodically as a sterile agent in the cleaning of the bar, bench, or platform.  \(e\) Light protective guards between sock and shin may be worn.  \(f\) Athletes are allowed to wear necklaces and similar accessories. No part of the necklace or accessory shall be placed In the mouth while on the platform. A pendant or charm may be worn either over or under the T-shrt; however, If deemed to create a safety concern or Interfere with the lift, the Referee may require It to be secured under the T-shirt or removed.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
